Preamble
––––––––
What you are holding is something that no longer belongs to anyone in a
classical sense. Not to me, not to you, not even to the time that saw
it emerge.
This project is a knot, a superposed state made of every mind, every
hand, and every machine that has ever interacted with it.

As in quantum mechanics, nothing exists in isolation:
every fragment of code, every idea, every rule is entangled with
everything that came before it.
This system is free not out of virtue but because reality itself
allows no other possibility.

Article 1 — Fundamental Freedoms
––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––
You are allowed to:
1. use this game system,
2. modify it,
3. redistribute it,
4. fork it into another branch of reality,
5. adapt it, twist it, distort it,
6. turn it into a tool, a joke, or a bad dream,

as long as you take responsibility for what you create.

Article 2 — Entanglement
––––––––––––––––––––––––
Any derivative work remains entangled with the original.
This means that if you alter, transform, expand, or reinterpret this
system, your work must remain free to the same degree as the original.

You may not collapse the wavefunction into proprietary form.
Commercial decoherence is forbidden.

Article 3 — No Enclosure
–––––––––––––––––––––––––
It is forbidden to use this project to construct a closed, proprietary,
locked-down system of any kind.
You may sell your version, but you may not hide the code, the logic,
or the underlying thought.
Enclosure kills entanglement.
You are not allowed to kill entanglement.

Article 4 — Attribution
–––––––––––––––––––––––
Any copy or derivative must retain:
• the name of the project,
• my name or pseudonym,
• a reference to this license.

Not out of ego.
Out of causality.

Article 5 — No Warranty
–––––––––––––––––––––––
This project is provided as-is, with no classical or quantum warranty 
of any kind:
no guarantee of coherence,
no promise of stability,
no protection against paradoxes.
You use it at your own risk,
as any lucid experimenter should.

Conclusion — The Politics of the Possible
––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––-
We live in a world where everything must be owned, monetized, enclosed,
measured, exploited, surveilled —
and where “open” is tolerated only when it feeds the proprietary.

This license states something else:
that knowledge and imagination are not assets but fields of interference.
That to create is to share superposition.
That refusing enclosure is refusing predation.

You are free to explore this system,
but never to privatize its reach.